{
  "schemaVersion": "1",
  "title": "review-offline: review a changeset in a local webpage",
  "summary": "A new skill that turns a PR, branch or diff into a local page. The invoking agent writes an animated graph of what the change does, a background Python server streams in headless correctness and cleanup suggestions, the reviewer accepts, edits and adds comments (or asks the agent), and Finish writes the accepted comments to a markdown file. Nothing is ever posted or edited upstream. The riskiest seam is the headless agent children: they read attacker-controlled diff text, so each host adapter locks them to read-only tools.",
